  speakerName: Aling Riza
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Language is more than words. Sometimes, it is about what you experience.

    In
    Ilokano, ''marikna'' means ''feel'' or ''perceive.''

    You can use it when
    talking about experiencing something through your senses or emotions.

    Now,
    try saying ''marikna'' yourself.'
